        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Beer - From Grain to Glass",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Malt Type | Kiln Temp | Color (SRM) | Enzymes | Flavor | Use |\n|-----------|-----------|-------------|---------|--------|-----|\n| Pale malt | 65-85 degrees C | 1.5-3 | Full enzymatic power | Biscuit, grain | Base malt; provides enzymes |\n| Vienna | 90 degrees C | 3-4 | Substantial | Light toast | Lager character |\n| Munich | 100-105 degrees C | 6-9 | Some | Malty, bread | Dark lager, Märzen |\n| Crystal/Caramel | Wet-kilned 65 degrees C + 150 degrees C | 10-120 | None | Sweet, caramel, toffee | Body, color, sweetness |\n| Chocolate | 200 degrees C | 350-450 | None | Coffee, chocolate | Stout, porter |\n| Black/Roasted | 220-230 degrees C | 500-600 | None | Roast, ash | Dry stout (Guinness character) |"
    },
